  "communities": {
    "0": "Build system, tooling & test-infra compatibility. Covers the bleeding-edge toolchain (AGP 9.x, Kotlin 2.2.10, KSP2, Hilt, compileSdk 37) where version coupling is non-obvious: Hilt>=2.59.2, KSP versioned independently of Kotlin, core-ktx needing compileSdk 37. Key risks: version-mismatch build crashes and JVM-vs-Android class availability (org.json). Also unit-test gotchas: real-time dispatchers in runTest and Room KSP overriding constructor defaults.",
    "1": "SFTP protocol & JSch (mwiede fork) client behavior. The core risk area: JSch RESUME mode stat()s the destination (local for download, remote for upload) so it throws on fresh transfers -> route by offset. ChannelSftp is not thread-safe (open a fresh channel per op). HostKey.getKey() returns base64. Established decision: use the mwiede fork (Terrapin-patched), never com.jcraft.",
    "2": "Background transfers: WorkManager foreground service, cache lifecycle & resumable pause/resume. Production-breaking risks: FGS type must be declared both at runtime (ForegroundInfo DATA_SYNC) and at install (manifest merge for SystemForegroundService); callbackFlow awaitClose hangs single-shot transfers (use close()); cache files must outlive the Worker and share naming across the ViewModel<->Worker boundary. Pause = stop worker + persist offset; retry = re-enqueue with offset reset.",
    "3": "Jetpack Compose UI & Storage Access Framework patterns. Covers ViewModel wiring (viewModel() + @HiltViewModel, no NavHost), mutableStateOf imports, launcher closure capture order, SAF display-name null fallback, multi-select via combinedClickable, and the file browser's raw-vs-derived list (pure FileView) with last-path memory across tabs.",
    "4": "Security: host-key trust (TOFU) & credential storage. Show SHA-256 fingerprints (not MD5), never StrictHostKeyChecking=no. Fingerprints are public keys -> plaintext JSON in DataStore; credentials are secrets -> Android Keystore AES-GCM (security-crypto is deprecated), stored separately from profiles. Post-connect verification returns a sealed HostKeyResult.",
    "5": "Persistence layer: DataStore & Room. DataStore holds connection profiles as a JSON blob and trusted hosts as a JSON list; Room (sftping.db) persists transfer state and doubles as the source of 'already uploaded' memory. Cross-ViewModel session data bridged via a @Singleton SessionState."
  }
